  "corrections_and_interpretation": [
    "B improves position MAE versus A in all four weightings, 288/300 scenes and 35/38 components, but point RMSE worsens by 490.82055m. Broad MAE improvement is not uniform position improvement.",
    "B versus adaptive076B lowers MAE by115.01134m but RMSE/P95/P99 all worsen; no full position ranking follows from MAE alone.",
    "B auxiliary speed MAE53.86216 is numerically close to the ordinary physical control53.8510, but mean errors do not establish equal predictions. Heading84.13232 remains worse than the physical control75.9364 and near its own random-head initial83.9824; the two auxiliary attributes cannot jointly be described as reverting to the physical prior.",
    "B own initial speed98.9172 is not076B final speed1.44243. The S2L title uses an inter-method comparison, not B temporal degradation.",
    "A is worse than adaptive076B in all three attribute MAEs; learning auxiliary heads relative to initialization is not evidence fixed weights shift a gain toward auxiliary tasks.",
    "Same position coefficient with auxiliary supervision removed identifies a trained-strategy difference in this matched run. It does not measure per-task gradient conflict, isolate sigma causality, or demonstrate a universal harm from multitask learning.",
    "B still has position MAE1494.04878 versus own fixed095 initial721.17448, so auxiliary supervision alone cannot account for failure of this PTFM adaptation.",
    "Window task coefficients are averaging factors, not gradients or Adam contributions; windows change sample populations, so declining window losses do not prove fixed-T convergence or generalization.",
    "The three original support regions are disjoint; helper-present/absent is a separate overlapping partition and their contributions must not be added to support-region contributions."
  ],
